[[1,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Use tool (1a) to lock the gear, unscrew the retaining bolt and\nremove gear (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.765.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2033892.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,0,"<p>1. Unscrew the retaining bolts.</p><p>2. Remove the oil seal cover on the auxiliary driveshaft.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2033893.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the cover in a vice, remove sealing ring (1a) by inserting\na drift in groove (1b) on the inner cover surface.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2033894.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,0,"<p>Position the cover on the engine crankcase\nin the auxiliary driveshaft.</p><p>Tighten the fixing bolts to torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>AUX SHAFT SEAL COVER</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.1</p></td></tr></table></div><p>1. Use tool (1a) to fit the new sealing ring (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Fitting tool</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.882.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2033895.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,0,"<p>Fit the gear on the auxiliary driveshaft.</p><p>Lock the pulley using the tool and screw\nin the pulley retaining bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>AUXILIARY SHAFT DRIVEN GEAR</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>8</p></td></tr></table></div>"]]